# PHP / Laravel layering

## Controllers
- Authorize, validate input, call a service/action, return view/JSON/redirect.
- Do not embed pricing rules, matching rules, or payment confirmation logic in controllers.

## Services / Support / Actions
- Own business rules and orchestration.
- Prefer extending an existing service over a parallel copy.
- Keep methods small; early return on invalid state.

## Models
- Persistence, relations, scopes, simple accessors.
- Avoid fat models that render HTML or call payment gateways directly (use services).

## Constants
- No scattered magic strings for statuses/roles when a class/enum/config already exists.
- Prefer existing enums/config in this repo over new ad-hoc string compares.

```php
// ❌ BAD — business + HTTP mixed
public function store(Request $request) {
    $amount = $request->price * 0.15; // commission buried here
    // ...
}

// ✅ GOOD — controller delegates
public function store(Request $request, BookingService $bookings) {
    $booking = $bookings->createFromRequest($request->validated());
    return redirect()->route('...', $booking);
}
```

## Reuse first
Search `app/Services`, `app/Support`, `app/Actions` (if present) before adding a new class.
